.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/10/Royally-Spooked-Event-Square_AD292D82-01CA-1817-BE8D9BAA60A97D8A_eve\r\n nts-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:cd4ac24b8b0dec7237260739e8f27d5c\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104627Z\r\nSUMMARY:Royally Spooked Halloween Pop-up at Royal Restaurant\r\nDESCRIPTION:This October\, Royal's patio is going spooky. Step onto our hau\r\n nted patio for Royally Spooked\, a Halloween pop-up filled with eerie déc\r\n or\, festive drinks\, and spooky-season vibes all month long. Gather your \r\n favorite ghosts and ghouls\, grab a cocktail\, and settle in for a royally\r\n  spooky good time at Royal Restaurant.\r\nURL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=660178&r\r\n estref=660178&experienceId=789237&lang=en-US&ot_source=Website&ot_campaign\r\n =Royal+Halloween+Pop-Up\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261029\r\nLOCATION:730 North Saint Asaph Street\r\nGEO:38.812738;-77.044362\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=730 North Saint Asaph Stree\r\n t;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=:geo:38.812738,-77.044362\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/10/Royally-Spooked-Event-Square_AD292D82-01CA-1817-BE8D9BAA60A97D8A_eve\r\n nts-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:b7eaf8639e32a3e56c05a17dc7159383\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104627Z\r\nSUMMARY:Royally Spooked Halloween Pop-up at Royal Restaurant\r\nDESCRIPTION:This October\, Royal's patio is going spooky. Step onto our hau\r\n nted patio for Royally Spooked\, a Halloween pop-up filled with eerie déc\r\n or\, festive drinks\, and spooky-season vibes all month long. Gather your \r\n favorite ghosts and ghouls\, grab a cocktail\, and settle in for a royally\r\n  spooky good time at Royal Restaurant.\r\nURL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=660178&r\r\n estref=660178&experienceId=789237&lang=en-US&ot_source=Website&ot_campaign\r\n =Royal+Halloween+Pop-Up\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030\r\nLOCATION:730 North Saint Asaph Street\r\nGEO:38.812738;-77.044362\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=730 North Saint Asaph Stree\r\n t;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=:geo:38.812738,-77.044362\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/10/Royally-Spooked-Event-Square_AD292D82-01CA-1817-BE8D9BAA60A97D8A_eve\r\n nts-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:24852a92ebc31d0cf87ac409089c32fc\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104652Z\r\nSUMMARY:30th Annual Del Ray Halloween Parade\r\nDESCRIPTION:One of Del Ray's favorite traditions\, the 30th Annual Del Ray \r\n Halloween Parade\, takes place on Sunday\, Oct. 25 at 2pm along Mount Vern\r\n on Avenue\, beginning at E. Bellefonte Avenue. Children\, pets\, and decor\r\n ated strollers are invited to march and show off their costumes! This para\r\n de ends with live music and an award presentation at the Mount Vernon Rec \r\n Center field. This hometown favorite\, named one of the 10 best Halloween \r\n parades in the country by USA Today\, is a must-see!\r\nURL:https://www.visitdelray.com/events/30th-annual-del-ray-halloween-parade\r\n /\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025\r\nLOCATION:E Bellefonte Ave\r\nGEO:38.823313;-77.056676\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=E Bellefonte Ave;X-APPLE-RA\r\n DIUS=49;X-TITLE=Del Ray Business Association:geo:38.823313,-77.056676\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/Del-Ray-Halloween-Parade-CREDIT-Will-Niccolls-1_4D450F16-BB2F-9830-D\r\n D1B1F6360638D02_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:67448ae110569d05ac1d8e270a4d8286\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104654Z\r\nSUMMARY:Trivia Night at Historic Sites - Halloween\r\nDESCRIPTION:Staff members at Carlyle House Historic Park combine their know\r\n ledge to create a spooky fun Trivia in honor of Halloween. Test your knowl\r\n edge on everything Halloween from general facts to movies to food.\nRegist\r\n ration must be done in advance. Limited capacity so register early!\nTicke\r\n ts are $15 per person and includes snacks and mocktails. Teams are limited\r\n  to 6 people. No outside alcohol is allowed. \n \nLink: http://apm.activ\r\n ecommunities.com/novaparks/Activity_Search/10375\r\nURL:http://apm.activecommunities.com/novaparks/Activity_Search/10375\r\nDTSTART:20261028T180000\r\nDTEND:20261028T200000\r\nLOCATION:121 N. Fairfax St.\r\nGEO:38.805197;-77.041793\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=121 N. Fairfax St.;X-APPLE-\r\n RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=:geo:38.805197,-77.041793\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/Trivia-Halloween-Marketing-2-_2EC2CDCE-4744-4703-A4FBA402C5B131D2_eve\r\n nts-150x150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:d2023f582cb5481574ab174c39240b02\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104650Z\r\nSUMMARY:Spooktacular Fit Crawl\r\nDESCRIPTION:Join us for the 4th Annual Spooktacular Fit Crawl - a fun-fille\r\n d fitness event with a spooky twist!Welcome to the Spooktacular Fit Crawl \r\n (4th Annual)!Your frightful afternoon will include a chilling cycle sessio\r\n n at Zweet Sport\, a Spooky Mat Pilates with Lalita Method\, and a bone-sh\r\n aking Yoga class with YOMEI. Each class will be 25 minutes long and space \r\n is limited to 8 people per group (3 groups available)! We encourage a true\r\n  crawl by either running or biking between locations! All ghoulish partici\r\n pants will receive a Spooky Swag bag\, with goodies and your very own meda\r\n l to commemorate your haunted experience!Join&#x85\;if you dare!!\r\nURL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1997482197022?aff=oddtdtcreator\r\nDTSTART:20261024T153000\r\nDTEND:20261024T173000\r\nLOCATION:727 N. Henry St.\r\nGEO:38.813370;-77.049385\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=727 N. Henry St.;X-APPLE-RA\r\n DIUS=49;X-TITLE=:geo:38.813370,-77.049385\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Zweet Sport;DIR=https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1997482197022?aff\r\n =oddtdtcreator:mailto:angela@zweetsport.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/2026-Spooktacular-Fit-Crawl-5-_149C4975-A0D3-C00F-9A10C5131EEFDCA5_ev\r\n ents-150x150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:e395b2c55befaaea3ac575e623891b3b\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104649Z\r\nSUMMARY:Specialty Tours: Preservation of Carlyle\r\nDESCRIPTION:In the 19th century\, James Green made renovations to John Carl\r\n yle's stone mansion to bring it up-to-date. When NOVA Parks purchased Carl\r\n yle House in 1970\, the decision was made to bring it back to Carlyle's 18\r\n th century mansion. Join our experts in an in depth exploration of the cha\r\n nges the architects made using photographs and artifacts. \n \nHaving tr\r\n ouble registering? Please call 703-549-2997 or email carlyle@nvrpa.org\n \r\n \nTicket Link: http://apm.activecommunities.com/novaparks/Activity_Search/\r\n 9840\r\nURL:http://apm.activecommunities.com/novaparks/Activity_Search/9840\r\nDTSTART:20261024T133000\r\nDTEND:20261024T150000\r\nLOCATION:121 N. Fairfax\r\nGEO:38.805197;-77.041793\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=121 N. Fairfax;X-APPLE-RADI\r\n US=49;X-TITLE=:geo:38.805197,-77.041793\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/SPECIALTY-TOURS-social-3-_1726C3DD-369C-4592-8272F64100D79D0C_events-\r\n 150x150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:0028015ab1a21060d7dc05cfe8a7d855\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104624Z\r\nSUMMARY:Gravestone Stories - Alexandria Historic Cemetery Complex - 13 Ceme\r\n teries Walking Tour\r\nDESCRIPTION:Go beyond King Street on a 90-minute guided walk through Alexan\r\n dria's remarkable Wilkes Street Cemetery Complex&#x97\;13 historic cemeter\r\n ies\, 52 acres\, and more than 35\,000 burials in one walkable landscape.\\r\n nLed by independent historian and cemetery superintendent David Heiby\, cr\r\n eator of Gravestone Stories\, the tour connects Alexandria's past to the A\r\n merican Revolution\, War of 1812\, Civil War\, Cold War\, and more. Meet G\r\n eorge Washington's pallbearers\, Revolutionary War patriots\, Civil War so\r\n ldiers\, a Soviet spy\, and others whose stories illuminate more than two \r\n centuries of Alexandria history.\nEvery stop is grounded in original resea\r\n rch\, cemetery records\, and discoveries made within the complex\, includi\r\n ng graves rediscovered after nearly 200 years.\nTours are limited to small\r\n  groups. The 90-minute walk covers approximately 1 to 1.5 miles over histo\r\n ric cemetery paths and uneven terrain. Free parking is available.\nTours a\r\n re offered Fridays and Saturdays at 1:00 p.m.\, with an additional Thursda\r\n y tour at 3:30 p.m. Tickets are $30 per person and include the official Gr\r\n avestone Stories companion e-book. See the Gravestone Stories website for \r\n current availability and booking.\r\nURL:https://www.viator.com/tours/Virginia/Journey-Through-Americas-Most-His\r\n toric-Cemetery-Complex/d22229-5589637P1\r\nDTSTART:20261029T153000\r\nDTEND:20261029T170000\r\nLOCATION:Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes Street\r\nGEO:38.801642;-77.056728\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes St\r\n reet;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Gravestone Stories:geo:38.801642,-77.056728\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Gravestone Stories;DIR=https://www.viator.com/tours/Virginia/J\r\n ourney-Through-Americas-Most-Historic-Cemetery-Complex/d22229-5589637P1:ma\r\n ilto:dave@gravestonestories.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/Image-3_82A3E35D-BECE-41ED-B5E2A50709C2E1EF_events-150x150.jpe\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:84d1076bce7f3084a445015483867b63\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104654Z\r\nSUMMARY:A Night of Women in Power and Poetry in honor of Kelly Grace Thomas\r\n 's Future Tense\r\nDESCRIPTION:Join Old Town Books for a special poetry reading and conversati\r\n on in honor of Kelly Grace Thomas' Future Tense.On Wednesday\, October 28 \r\n at 7PM we are very excited to welcome three local poets\, Hannah Grieco\, \r\n Courtney LeBlanc\, and Jillian Stacia\, along with Kelly Grace Thomas for \r\n a reading and panel event!Hannah Grieco is the author of "First Kicking\, \r\n Then Not\," out now from Stanchion Books. She writes a literary column for\r\n  Washington City Paper\, edits prose at a variety of small presses and lit\r\n erary journals\, and teaches literature at Marymount University. Read her \r\n work in The Washington Post\, Al Jazeera\, The Rumpus\, Brevity\, Wigleaf\\r\n , Shenandoah\, Poet Lore\, Fairy Tale Review\, and more. Find her at www.h\r\n grieco.com.Courtney LeBlanc is the author of the four full-length collecti\r\n ons\, most recently Her Dark Everything and Her Whole Bright Life (winner \r\n of the Jack McCarthy Book Prize). She is the Arlington County Poet Laureat\r\n e Emerita and the founder and editor-in-chief of Riot in Your Throat\, an \r\n independent poetry press. She's also the founder of the Poetry Coven\, a m\r\n onthly generative workshop. She loves pitbulls\, tattoos\, and a soy latte\r\n  each morning. Find her online at www.courtneyleblanc.com.Jillian Stacia i\r\n s the author of the poetry collection\, SET THE BONE\, published by Arcana\r\n  Poetry Press. She was selected as an Honorable Mention for the 2025 Jack \r\n McCarthy Book Prize and short-listed for the 2026 Central Avenue Poetry Pr\r\n ize. She has been nominated for several awards\, including 2025 Best of Ne\r\n t and the 2025 Pushcart Prize. Her poetry has been featured in several lit\r\n erary magazines and anthologies. Find her online @jillianstacia to read mo\r\n re of her work.Kelly Grace Thomas\, poet\, writer\, and coach\, is the aut\r\n hor of Future Tense (Alice James Books\, 2026) and Boat Burned (YesYes Boo\r\n ks\, 2020). She's the winner of the Neil Postman Award for Metaphor from R\r\n attle. Her poems appear in: The Sun\, The Adroit Journal\, 32 Poems\, Sixt\r\n h Finch\, and elsewhere. She is the co-author of Words Ignite: Explore\, W\r\n rite\, and Perform Classic and Spoken Word Poetry\, taught in the Los Ange\r\n les Unified School District. She holds an MFA from Randolph College. Kelly\r\n  lives in Benicia\, California\, where she coaches writers online. www.kel\r\n lygracethomas.com\r\nURL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/a-night-of-women-in-power-and-poetry-in-ho\r\n nor-of-future-tense-tickets-1997622022243\r\nDTSTART:20261028T190000\r\nDTEND:20261028T203000\r\nLOCATION:130 S. Royal Street\r\nGEO:38.803640;-77.043689\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=130 S. Royal Street;X-APPLE\r\n -RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Old Town Books:geo:38.803640,-77.043689\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/10_events.28-Poetry-Panel-1-_E0F41041-E736-2D20-D21057BAB55F976A-150x\r\n 150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:0f2fcc1534612e872b5d914d78c728bc\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104624Z\r\nSUMMARY:Alexandria Historic Cemetery Complex: 13 Cemeteries Walking Tour\r\nDESCRIPTION:Go beyond King Street on a 90-minute guided walk through Alexan\r\n dria's remarkable Wilkes Street Cemetery Complex&#x97\;13 historic cemeter\r\n ies\, 52 acres\, and more than 35\,000 burials in one walkable landscape.L\r\n ed by independent historian and cemetery superintendent David Heiby\, crea\r\n tor of Gravestone Stories\, the tour connects Alexandria's past to the Ame\r\n rican Revolution\, War of 1812\, Civil War\, Cold War\, and more. Meet Geo\r\n rge Washington's pallbearers\, Revolutionary War patriots\, Civil War sold\r\n iers\, a Soviet spy\, and others whose stories illuminate more than two ce\r\n nturies of Alexandria history.\nEvery stop is grounded in original researc\r\n h\, cemetery records\, and discoveries made within the complex\, including\r\n  graves rediscovered after nearly 200 years.\nTours are limited to small g\r\n roups. The 90-minute walk covers approximately 1 to 1.5 miles over histori\r\n c cemetery paths and uneven terrain. Free parking is available.Tours are o\r\n ffered Fridays and Saturdays at 1:00 p.m.\, with an additional Thursday to\r\n ur at 3:30 p.m. Tickets are $30 per person and include the official Graves\r\n tone Stories companion e-book. See the Gravestone Stories website for curr\r\n ent availability and booking.\r\nURL:https://www.viator.com/tours/Virginia/Journey-Through-Americas-Most-His\r\n toric-Cemetery-Complex/d22229-5589637P1\r\nDTSTART:20261024T130000\r\nDTEND:20261024T143000\r\nLOCATION:Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes Street\r\nGEO:38.801642;-77.056728\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes St\r\n reet;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Gravestone Stories:geo:38.801642,-77.056728\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Gravestone Stories;DIR=https://www.viator.com/tours/Virginia/J\r\n ourney-Through-Americas-Most-Historic-Cemetery-Complex/d22229-5589637P1:ma\r\n ilto:dave@gravestonestories.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/Image-3_7EDF5B00-0BDF-D085-D8474A1FAD39DD47_events-150x150.jpe\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:f38734e2348d70cad919668d920d9744\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104624Z\r\nSUMMARY:Alexandria Historic Cemetery Complex: 13 Cemeteries Walking Tour\r\nDESCRIPTION:Go beyond King Street on a 90-minute guided walk through Alexan\r\n dria's remarkable Wilkes Street Cemetery Complex&#x97\;13 historic cemeter\r\n ies\, 52 acres\, and more than 35\,000 burials in one walkable landscape.L\r\n ed by independent historian and cemetery superintendent David Heiby\, crea\r\n tor of Gravestone Stories\, the tour connects Alexandria's past to the Ame\r\n rican Revolution\, War of 1812\, Civil War\, Cold War\, and more. Meet Geo\r\n rge Washington's pallbearers\, Revolutionary War patriots\, Civil War sold\r\n iers\, a Soviet spy\, and others whose stories illuminate more than two ce\r\n nturies of Alexandria history.\nEvery stop is grounded in original researc\r\n h\, cemetery records\, and discoveries made within the complex\, including\r\n  graves rediscovered after nearly 200 years.\nTours are limited to small g\r\n roups. The 90-minute walk covers approximately 1 to 1.5 miles over histori\r\n c cemetery paths and uneven terrain. Free parking is available.Tours are o\r\n ffered Fridays and Saturdays at 1:00 p.m.\, with an additional Thursday to\r\n ur at 3:30 p.m. Tickets are $30 per person and include the official Graves\r\n tone Stories companion e-book. See the Gravestone Stories website for curr\r\n ent availability and booking.\r\nURL:https://www.viator.com/tours/Virginia/Journey-Through-Americas-Most-His\r\n toric-Cemetery-Complex/d22229-5589637P1\r\nDTSTART:20261030T130000\r\nDTEND:20261030T143000\r\nLOCATION:Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes Street\r\nGEO:38.801642;-77.056728\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes St\r\n reet;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Gravestone Stories:geo:38.801642,-77.056728\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Gravestone Stories;DIR=https://www.viator.com/tours/Virginia/J\r\n ourney-Through-Americas-Most-Historic-Cemetery-Complex/d22229-5589637P1:ma\r\n ilto:dave@gravestonestories.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/Image-3_7EDF5B00-0BDF-D085-D8474A1FAD39DD47_events-150x150.jpe\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:2f49e3a2a0c16ab4c91f0ed1a8e4da09\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104700Z\r\nSUMMARY:Lee-Fendall: Haunted Lantern Tours\r\nDESCRIPTION:Tour the historic Lee-Fendall House at night by lantern light! \r\n Learn about the history of the home on this spooky\, guided experience.\nT\r\n ake a tour of the historic Lee-Fendall House at night! A quieter\, cozier \r\n experience in Old Town Alexandria\, this tour covers the history of the ho\r\n use and the ghostly stories from within its walls. As you are led through \r\n the first and second floors of the home by the light of lantern\, you migh\r\n t just hear or see something spooky along the way.\nHaunted Lantern Tours \r\n will be at 7:00pm &amp\; 8:00pm on October 30th &amp\; 31st.\nThe lantern \r\n tours are recommended for ages 12+. Each tour time is limited to 12 people\r\n .\nTickets are $20 per person. The tour last about 45 minutes.\r\nURL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/haunted-lantern-tour-tickets-1998105557510\r\n ?aff=oddtdtcreator\r\nDTSTART:20261030T190000\r\nDTEND:20261030T210000\r\nLOCATION:614 Oronoco Street\r\nGEO:38.809419;-77.045740\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=614 Oronoco Street;X-APPLE-\r\n RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Lee-Fendall House Museum & Garden:geo:38.809419,-77.0457\r\n 40\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Lee-Fendall House Museum & Garden;DIR=https://www.eventbrite.c\r\n om/e/haunted-lantern-tour-tickets-1998105557510?aff=oddtdtcreator:mailto:c\r\n ontact@leefendallhouse.org\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/Lantern-Tours_328F2125-D3B3-4830-BA376F9BD3613203_events-150x150.jpe\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:a068b042b2ced1cdcfbc48d2f86c76e5\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104649Z\r\nSUMMARY:Specialty Tours: Preservation of Carlyle\r\nDESCRIPTION:In the 19th century\, James Green made renovations to John Carl\r\n yle's stone mansion to bring it up-to-date. When NOVA Parks purchased Carl\r\n yle House in 1970\, the decision was made to bring it back to Carlyle's 18\r\n th century mansion. Join our experts in an in depth exploration of the cha\r\n nges the architects made using photographs and artifacts. \nHaving troubl\r\n e registering? Please call 703-549-2997 or email carlyle@nvrpa.org\n \r\nURL:http://apm.activecommunities.com/novaparks/Activity_Search/9840\r\nDTSTART:20261024T133000\r\nDTEND:20261024T150000\r\nLOCATION:121 N Fairfax St\r\nGEO:38.805197;-77.041793\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=121 N Fairfax St;X-APPLE-RA\r\n DIUS=49;X-TITLE=:geo:38.805197,-77.041793\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/SPECIALTY-TOURS-social-2-_0B9BBA3B-8963-454F-A93978A8CB4FB179_events-\r\n 150x150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:f270fbc8929f49f2802cb784e7630f18\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104642Z\r\nSUMMARY:Death Comes to Carlyle House\r\nDESCRIPTION:In September 1780\, John Carlyle passed away and the family wou\r\n ld have gone into mourning. Join our tour guides for one night only to lea\r\n rn about death and mourning in the 18th century. Tours will be self paced \r\n and visitors can enter the house starting at 6pm with the last entry at 7:\r\n 45pm. \nHaving trouble registering? Please call 703-549-2997 or email car\r\n lyle@nvrpa.org. \nTicket link: http://apm.activecommunities.com/novaparks\r\n /Activity_Search/10354 \r\nURL:https://www.novaparks.com/parks/carlyle-house-historic-park\r\nDTSTART:20261024T180000\r\nDTEND:20261024T200000\r\nLOCATION:121 N Fairfax St\r\nGEO:38.805197;-77.041793\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=121 N Fairfax St;X-APPLE-RA\r\n DIUS=49;X-TITLE=:geo:38.805197,-77.041793\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/Death-Comes-to-Carlyle-Marketing_E0FFAEE1-4511-4435-A45C57E1ADA245C4_\r\n events-150x150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:f6c53d677d8b13e1f77ca426f294c005\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104658Z\r\nSUMMARY:The Lyceum: Poe in Alexandria\r\nDESCRIPTION:Poe in Alexandria\nDon't miss an unforgettable evening with Ame\r\n rica's earliest master of the macabre - Edgar Allan Poe! Actor David Keltz\r\n  returns to The Lyceum's lecture hall to re-create Poe's visit to Virginia\r\n  in 1849\, shortly before his death. This year's performance will include \r\n short stories\, poems\, musings\, and literary criticism. Mr. Keltz's perf\r\n ormance has been lauded by The Poe House and Museum in Baltimore\, The Poe\r\n  Museum in Richmond\, and the Poe National Historic Site in Philadelphia. \r\n Reservations strongly recommended. Doors open at 7:15 p.m.\, performance b\r\n egins at 8 p.m. Wine and beer bar will be available before the show (credi\r\n t and cash accepted). Tickets available online at https://shop.alexandria\r\n va.gov/Events.aspx\r\nURL:https://shop.alexandriava.gov/Events.aspx\r\nDTSTART:20261029T200000\r\nDTEND:20261029T211500\r\nLOCATION:201 S. Washington Street\r\nGEO:38.803764;-77.047586\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=201 S. Washington Street;X-\r\n APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Alexandria History Museum at The Lyceum:geo:38.803\r\n 764,-77.047586\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/E6000043_1-1-_270C5FB9-CC71-4959-A7FB7059FB6B6B38_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:f2225e01101b905875927177c9ec17b4\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104658Z\r\nSUMMARY:The Lyceum: Poe in Alexandria\r\nDESCRIPTION:Poe in Alexandria\nDon't miss an unforgettable evening with Ame\r\n rica's earliest master of the macabre - Edgar Allan Poe! Actor David Keltz\r\n  returns to The Lyceum's lecture hall to re-create Poe's visit to Virginia\r\n  in 1849\, shortly before his death. This year's performance will include \r\n short stories\, poems\, musings\, and literary criticism. Mr. Keltz's perf\r\n ormance has been lauded by The Poe House and Museum in Baltimore\, The Poe\r\n  Museum in Richmond\, and the Poe National Historic Site in Philadelphia. \r\n Reservations strongly recommended. Doors open at 7:15 p.m.\, performance b\r\n egins at 8 p.m. Wine and beer bar will be available before the show (credi\r\n t and cash accepted). Tickets available online at https://shop.alexandria\r\n va.gov/Events.aspx\r\nURL:https://shop.alexandriava.gov/Events.aspx\r\nDTSTART:20261030T200000\r\nDTEND:20261030T211500\r\nLOCATION:201 S. Washington Street\r\nGEO:38.803764;-77.047586\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=201 S. Washington Street;X-\r\n APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Alexandria History Museum at The Lyceum:geo:38.803\r\n 764,-77.047586\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/E6000043_1-1-_270C5FB9-CC71-4959-A7FB7059FB6B6B38_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:67c0f9c4f78461c9cc1af7f9222cd808\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104628Z\r\nSUMMARY:Specialty Tour: Poisons at the Apothecary Museum\r\nDESCRIPTION:Specialty Tour: Poisons at the Apothecary Museum \nExplore the\r\n  sinister side of medicine on the Apothecary Museum's Poisons Tour. This o\r\n ne-hour tour explores several different types of poisons\, their historic \r\n uses at the Apothecary\, and what we know today. Recommended for adults. T\r\n our is 6-7pm. Please arrive a few minutes early to check-in. The doors wil\r\n l be locked once the tour begins.\r\nURL:https://shop.alexandriava.gov/Events.aspx\r\nDTSTART:20261030T180000\r\nDTEND:20261030T190000\r\nLOCATION:105-107 S. Fairfax Street\r\nGEO:38.804246;-77.042751\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=105-107 S. Fairfax Street;X\r\n -APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Stabler-Leadbeater Apothecary Museum:geo:38.80424\r\n 6,-77.042751\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/E6000550_1_F0F422C4-5578-4D87-B1D272068B60686E_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:34521d84b028a1eae12adcb2f6b5ab23\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104643Z\r\nSUMMARY:George Washington's Mount Vernon: Fall Harvest Family Days\r\nDESCRIPTION:Celebrate the crisp autumn season with 18th-century activities \r\n and demonstrations at the Farm at Mount Vernon.\nWatch wheat treading demo\r\n nstrations in George Washington's innovative 16-sided threshing barn and m\r\n eet Mount Vernon's farm animals.\nPlus\, watch demonstrations of cooking\,\r\n  textiles\, laundry\, and learn how equipment was made in the 18th century\r\n \, such as fish nets\, horseshoes\, and soap.\nThis event is sponsored by \r\n Dominion Energy.\r\nURL:https://www.mountvernon.org/plan-your-visit/calendar/events/fall-harves\r\n t-festival?utm_source=visitalexandria.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign\r\n =fall_harvest_fest_ec\r\nDTSTART:20261024T093000\r\nDTEND:20261024T163000\r\nLOCATION:3200 Mount Vernon Memorial Highway\r\nGEO:38.710402;-77.087024\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3200 Mount Vernon Memorial \r\n Highway;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=George Washington's Mount Vernon:geo:38.\r\n 710402,-77.087024\r\nORGANIZER;CN=George Washington's Mount Vernon;DIR=https://www.mountvernon.o\r\n rg/plan-your-visit/calendar/events/fall-harvest-festival?utm_source=visita\r\n lexandria.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=fall_harvest_fest_ec:mailto\r\n :tickets@mountvernon.org\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/MDP_20211023_DC-177_1CBF2A15-CC65-49FD-A2B935DAFEE8776C_events-150x1\r\n 50.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:92b465c638757460cfdd95baec897c2d\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104643Z\r\nSUMMARY:George Washington's Mount Vernon: Fall Harvest Family Days\r\nDESCRIPTION:Celebrate the crisp autumn season with 18th-century activities \r\n and demonstrations at the Farm at Mount Vernon.\nWatch wheat treading demo\r\n nstrations in George Washington's innovative 16-sided threshing barn and m\r\n eet Mount Vernon's farm animals.\nPlus\, watch demonstrations of cooking\,\r\n  textiles\, laundry\, and learn how equipment was made in the 18th century\r\n \, such as fish nets\, horseshoes\, and soap.\nThis event is sponsored by \r\n Dominion Energy.\r\nURL:https://www.mountvernon.org/plan-your-visit/calendar/events/fall-harves\r\n t-festival?utm_source=visitalexandria.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign\r\n =fall_harvest_fest_ec\r\nDTSTART:20261025T093000\r\nDTEND:20261025T163000\r\nLOCATION:3200 Mount Vernon Memorial Highway\r\nGEO:38.710402;-77.087024\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3200 Mount Vernon Memorial \r\n Highway;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=George Washington's Mount Vernon:geo:38.\r\n 710402,-77.087024\r\nORGANIZER;CN=George Washington's Mount Vernon;DIR=https://www.mountvernon.o\r\n rg/plan-your-visit/calendar/events/fall-harvest-festival?utm_source=visita\r\n lexandria.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=fall_harvest_fest_ec:mailto\r\n :tickets@mountvernon.org\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/MDP_20211023_DC-177_1CBF2A15-CC65-49FD-A2B935DAFEE8776C_events-150x1\r\n 50.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:99742e07a262a70b16539389f340df1c\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104642Z\r\nSUMMARY:George Washington Whiskey Dinner\r\nDESCRIPTION:Welcome the fall season at the historic Mount Vernon Inn Restau\r\n rant with a whiskey tasting and a 4-course meal. Experience the warmth of \r\n 3 styles of whiskey distilled at George Washington's Distillery &amp\; Gri\r\n stmill.\nMust be 21 or older to participate.\nView the menu and book a res\r\n ervation online or by phone.\r\nURL:https://www.mountvernonrestaurant.com/event/george-washingtons-whiskey-\r\n dinner?utm_source=visitalexandria.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=mv_\r\n inn_events_ec\r\nDTSTART:20261024T180000\r\nDTEND:20261024T210000\r\nLOCATION:3200 Mount Vernon Memorial Highway\r\nGEO:38.710439;-77.086961\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3200 Mount Vernon Memorial \r\n Highway;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Mount Vernon Inn:geo:38.710439,-77.08696\r\n 1\r\nORGANIZER;CN=George Washington's Mount Vernon;DIR=https://www.mountvernonre\r\n staurant.com/event/george-washingtons-whiskey-dinner?utm_source=visitalexa\r\n ndria.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=mv_inn_events_ec:mailto:tickets\r\n @mountvernon.org\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/george-washington-rye-whiskey-varieties-mount-vernon_4DC90113-0CF8-4\r\n 8CC-8181A368DAFBA62C_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:399887d5af851239edbf19fde4244cb2\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104634Z\r\nSUMMARY:Woodlawn & Pope-Leighey House: Canopy of Discovery\r\nDESCRIPTION:Experiencing history through outdoor mindfulness at Woodlawn &a\r\n mp\; Pope-Leighey House.\nAbout the Session:\nThe sessions are approximate\r\n ly 90-minutes long and are conducted in relative silence. They include war\r\n m-ups\, centering\, and breathing exercises to connect participants to the\r\n ir bodies and the world around them. These are followed by a walk and an e\r\n xtended sit which encourages participants to become more fully open and pr\r\n esent to their surroundings. We conclude with a returning ritual and a cha\r\n nce to reflect on the experience. This time in nature will not be strenuou\r\n s\; most abilities can be accommodated. All ages are welcomed but children\r\n  under 16 must be accompanied by an adult. \nImportant Arrival &amp\; Che\r\n ck-In Details\n\nCheck-In Location: All participants must check in at Wood\r\n lawn\, regardless of session topic.\nTiming: Sessions start promptly at 12\r\n :00 PM (Sundays). Please arrive early to ensure a timely start.\nDuration:\r\n  Approximately 90 minutes.\n\nFall Schedule &amp\; Locations\n\nSunday\, O\r\n ctober 11 | Woodlawn\nSunday\, October 25 | Pope-Leighey House\nSunday\, N\r\n ovember 1 | Woodlawn\nSunday\, November 8 | Pope-Leighey House\n\nTickets \r\n &amp\; Policies\n\nPrice: $30 per ticket. All purchases directly support t\r\n he preservation of this historic site.\nWeather: Programs take place rain \r\n or shine.\r\nURL:https://www.woodlawnpopeleighey.org/upcomingevents\r\nDTSTART:20261025T120000\r\nDTEND:20261025T133000\r\nLOCATION:9000 Richmond Highway\r\nGEO:38.718222;-77.137099\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=9000 Richmond Highway;X-APP\r\n LE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Woodlawn & Pope-Leighey House:geo:38.718222,-77.13709\r\n 9\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Woodlawn & Pope-Leighey House;DIR=https://www.woodlawnpopeleig\r\n hey.org/upcomingevents:mailto:woodlawn@savingplaces.org\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/Canopy-of-Discovery_293DBCE0-E371-4F87-99EF101157E71B5B_events-150x15\r\n 0.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:811ebf70e1faeeb173fb968d7c06feec\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104659Z\r\nSUMMARY:Halloween Decorations Bike Tour of Alexandria\r\nDESCRIPTION:Join us for a spook-tacular evening ride through the Del Ray an\r\n d Rosemont neighborhoods to check out the best Halloween decorations. This\r\n  family-friendly group ride will cover approximately 6 miles at a casual p\r\n ace\, with 8-10 stops to admire creative displays\, snap photos\, and enjo\r\n y the Halloween spirit.The ride will begin and end at the Main Line Boulev\r\n ard cul-de-sac and is open to riders of all ages and abilities. Bring ligh\r\n ts for your bike\, dress for the weather &#x96\; costumes highly encourage\r\n d!\r\nURL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/bpac-halloween-decorations-tour-2026-ticke\r\n ts-2000210084206\r\nDTSTART:20261030T180000\r\nDTEND:20261030T193000\r\nLOCATION:1000 Main Line Boulevard\r\nGEO:38.817076;-77.053130\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=1000 Main Line Boulevard;X-\r\n APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=1000 Main Line Boulevard\, Alexandria\, VA:geo:38.\r\n 817076,-77.053130\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/Halloween_Bike_Tour_Horizontal_Under_10MB_42A38C68-E820-31C7-C853FDC\r\n 55FD30D4F_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:2cc58b65f5cbb7a4e49a62dcdcf9635d\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104700Z\r\nSUMMARY:Local Historian Book Signing at the Alexandria Visitor Center\r\nDESCRIPTION:Meet historian Madeline Feierstein and grab a copy of her new b\r\n ook\, Occupied Alexandria: How the Civil War Transformed a Southern City\\r\n , at the Alexandria Visitor Center!\nThe day after Virginia's secession in\r\n  May 1861\, Union troops marched from Washington to occupy its neighbor Al\r\n exandria. A former powerhouse in the slave trade\, Alexandria was the firs\r\n t Confederate city in Virginia to be occupied during the Civil War and gov\r\n erned under strict martial law. Overnight\, this bustling urban town on th\r\n e Potomac River transformed into a center of disease\, death\, and debauch\r\n ery. Viewing all residents as potential threats regardless of allegiance\,\r\n  the military government resorted to heavy-handed actions to control its t\r\n ransient soldier population\, counteract civilian opposition\, combat wave\r\n s of gunshot wounds and illness\, and imprison those deemed disloyal to th\r\n e Union cause. Drawing upon true accounts of civilian and soldier experien\r\n ces\, historian Madeline Feierstein explores whether Union authorities kep\r\n t order within the city or watched it fall into chaos.\r\nURL:https://www.madelinefeierstein.com/\r\nDTSTART:20261030T140000\r\nDTEND:20261030T170000\r\nLOCATION:221 King Street\r\nGEO:38.804632;-77.042352\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=221 King Street;X-APPLE-RAD\r\n IUS=49;X-TITLE=Alexandria Visitor Center:geo:38.804632,-77.042352\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/09/Occupied-Alexandria-1030-Book-Signing-Event_D5992137-E1A7-448F-9300D2\r\n 8FC95E5208_events-150x150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:c3b30713225de51d2ae738532f9a6407\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104646Z\r\nSUMMARY:Old Town Trick-or-Treat 2026\r\nDESCRIPTION:Old Town Trick-or-Treat - Hosted by Pippin Toy Co. \nFor more t\r\n han a decade Old Town Alexandria has rolled out the red - or in this case \r\n orange - carpet to trick or treaters from all over the DMV. With the closi\r\n ng of Old Town Business\, this year\, Pippin Toy Co. is stepping in to kee\r\n p this beloved tradition alive. On October 24\, start at Pippin Toy Co.\, \r\n 1310 King St.\, to grab your map. Then spend the day trick or treating at \r\n some of your favorite businesses and historic attractions while enjoying a\r\n ll the thrills and chills Old Town Alexandria\, the DMV's Halloween hub\, \r\n has to offer. Old Town Trick-or-Treat\, Halloween Trick-or-Treating for th\r\n e littlest ghouls and goblins.\nWHEN: October 24 2026 at 11am to 4pm ET\nW\r\n HERE: Old Town Alexandria\nHighlights include:\n\nThe weekend of the event\r\n \, enjoy strolling the streets of Old Town\, Trick-or-Treating at your fav\r\n orite local businesses and historic locations.\nFree to participate\nPick \r\n up your map at Pippin Toy Co.\, 1310 King St.\nParticipating locations inc\r\n lude Red Barn Mercantile\, Penny Post\, Pippin Toy Co.\, Pacers Running\, \r\n Made in ALX\, 529 Kids Consign\, Mint Condition\, Eries Interiors\, Nothin\r\n g In Between Studio\, Mudhouse Coffee\, Ms. Moxie's Moon Shop\, Old Town B\r\n ooks\, AR Workshop Alexandria\, The World Crafted on King\, Long Dark Hous\r\n e\, ERA\, Pure Barre Alexandria\, Lowery's Dial\, The Spice and Tea Exchan\r\n ge\, Interior Instincts\, The Old Town Shop\, Eliana Curated\, Lee-Fendell\r\n  House Museum and Garden\, Boxwood\, Salon deZEN\, Visit Alexandria Visito\r\n r's Center\, Carlyle House Historic Site\, Alexandria History Museum at Th\r\n e Lyceum\nParticipants can expect drink specials for young and old alike a\r\n t Mudhouse Coffee andfun activations for kids at The Spice and Tea Exchang\r\n e\, Lowery's Dial\, and Lee-FendallHouse Museum and Garden.\r\nURL:https://pippintoyco.com/\r\nDTSTART:20261024T110000\r\nDTEND:20261024T160000\r\nLOCATION:1310 King Street\r\nGEO:38.805646;-77.054155\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=1310 King Street;X-APPLE-RA\r\n DIUS=49;X-TITLE=Pippin Toy Co.:geo:38.805646,-77.054155\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/09/Pippin-Toy-Co-2023-CREDIT-Pippin-Toy-Co-15_14C48070-B701-82A2-D6FFD2\r\n 98BDFB2AAA_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:7da4c9dd46169bc121598b32127dee9e\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104622Z\r\nSUMMARY:King Street Station Farmers Market\r\nDESCRIPTION:Join us for the King Street Station Farmers Market! Whether you\r\n 're a local resident\, a nearby employee looking for a mid-week break\, or\r\n  a commuter passing through\, this weekly market is the perfect way to spe\r\n nd your Wednesday afternoon.Featuring an incredible lineup of local and re\r\n gional farmers\, producers\, and artisans\, you can shop fresh produce alo\r\n ngside delicious baked goods\, wonderful self-care gifts\, and many more..\r\n Unwind on the plaza with a live busker performance while you browse. The m\r\n arket is family-friendly\, interactive\, and completely free to attend. Wh\r\n en: Wednesdays\, September 9 &#x96\; October 28\, 2026 (September 9\, 16\,\r\n  23\, 30\; October 7\, 14\, 21\, 28) | 3:00 PM &#x96\; 7:00 PMWhere: King \r\n Street Station\, 1800 Diagonal Road (On the center Plaza surrounding the f\r\n ountain)Meet Our MerchantsWe have a spectacular lineup of local vendors br\r\n inging premium products to your doorstep:Pleitez Produce Farm\, LLC Blacks\r\n tone Honey Bee Farms LLC Common Hearth Bakery Handmade by LMAC Judymakesju\r\n ices Ooh So Good Desserts Saint Rocco's Dog Treats Virginia Spores CalmCon\r\n nectWell Self Care Gifts (Drop-In)Dee-Lightfully Soft/Good (Drop-In) GC Af\r\n rican Creations (Drop-In) Julie Gross Artist (Drop-In) Keep an eye out for\r\n  more merchants to be announced soon!\r\nURL:https://eventeny.com/events/king-street-station-farmers-market-2026-297\r\n 27/\r\nDTSTART:20261028T150000\r\nDTEND:20261028T190000\r\nLOCATION:1236 Tennessee Dr NE\r\nGEO:39.118006;-77.534896\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=1236 Tennessee Dr NE;X-APPL\r\n E-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=1800 Diagonal Road:geo:39.118006,-77.534896\r\nORGANIZER;CN=VVS Evvent and Marketin