ath-revolutionary-war-encampm\r\n ent?utm_source=visitalexandria.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=estate\r\n _revwar_encamp_ec:mailto:tickets@mountvernon.org\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/03/0Q-yAnAV_AF0814F7-ABCF-4289-BE54B974948CA3D8_events-150x150.jpe\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:cd9371a9d31dff81c2ed397e0e06ae02\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104606Z\r\nSUMMARY:Monthly Public Tour\r\nDESCRIPTION:Join the public tour of the Basilica of Saint Mary\, on the 4th\r\n  Monday of every month at 6pm. Tours meet outside the front entrance of th\r\n e church and last approximately 45 minutes.\nInterested in scheduling a pr\r\n ivate tour? Call the parish office at 703-836-4100.\r\nURL:http://stmaryoldtown.org\r\nDTSTART:20261026T180000\r\nDTEND:20261026T184500\r\nLOCATION:310 S. Royal Street\r\nGEO:38.801890;-77.043821\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=310 S. Royal Street;X-APPLE\r\n -RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=The Basilica of Saint Mary:geo:38.801890,-77.043821\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Basilica of Saint Mary;DIR=http://stmaryoldtown.org:mailto:vny\r\n ce@stmaryoldtown.org\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/03/BasilicaFront2_575E88E0-D625-4646-8FA9B3F9A5847516_events-150x150.jp\r\n e\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:f880871e55ae954f1bcef2a22386c743\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104607Z\r\nSUMMARY:Tabletop Takeover\r\nDESCRIPTION:Roll the dice\, shuffle the deck\, and let the games begin!\nJo\r\n in us on the last Sunday of every month for Tabletop Takeover at Port City\r\n  Brewing Co. Starting at 3pm\, we'll set aside tables in our Indoor Beer G\r\n arden for an afternoon of board games\, card games\, puzzles\, dominoes\, \r\n and more. We'll have a great selection of games ready to go\, so you can j\r\n ump in with friends&#x97\;old and new&#x97\;or bring along your favorite g\r\n ame to share and teach. \nCold beer\, good company\, and friendly competi\r\n tion guaranteed!\r\nURL:https://www.portcitybrewing.com/\r\nDTSTART:20261025T150000\r\nDTEND:20261025T190000\r\nLOCATION:3950 Wheeler Avenue\r\nGEO:38.807998;-77.101501\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3950 Wheeler Avenue;X-APPLE\r\n -RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Port City Brewing Company:geo:38.807998,-77.101501\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Port City Brewing Company;DIR=https://www.portcitybrewing.com/\r\n :mailto:ryan@portcitybrewing.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/02/TableTopTakeover-1920-x-1080-px-_686668C2-45F1-4828-B84EC5F59CC37ADB_\r\n events-150x150.png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:30e14bed1c0f4fedd439aba8728a11cb\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104604Z\r\nSUMMARY:Pedals & Pints - Long Ride\r\nDESCRIPTION:Pedals &amp\; Pints will get you hopped up on cycling!   Port \r\n City and Handy Bikes have teamed up to co-host approachable\, fun\, no-dro\r\n p group rides twice a month.  Pedals &amp\; Pints rides depart from Handy\r\n  Bikes retail showroom at 3800 Wheeler Ave\, and end at Port City Brewing \r\n at 3950 Wheeler Ave.  \nThere are two rides to choose from:\nShort Ride: \r\n  2nd Saturday of each month -- A punchy 10 mile ride\, departing the reta\r\n il showroom at 10:30am.  Avg pace 10mph\, no drop.   A few steep but sho\r\n rt hills.  Returns to Port City &amp\; La Tingeria for beer and/or tacos \r\n around 12pm.\nLong Ride:  4th Saturday of each month -- A 20-30 mile vary\r\n ing route\, departing the retail showroom at 10:30am.  Avg pace 12-14mph\\r\n , no drop\; expect several moderate hills. Returns to Port City &amp\; La \r\n Tingeria for beer and/or tacos around 12:30-1pm.\nRiders of all ages who h\r\n ave the confidence and skill to participate in a group ride setting are in\r\n vited.  Road bikes and flashing lights are encouraged\; helmets are manda\r\n tory.  E-bikes (class 1\, 2\, or 3 only) are welcome at all rides.  Rout\r\n es may include sections of road that do not have protected bike lanes.  A\r\n ll participants must sign a waiver before riding.\nFor more information an\r\n d to RSVP for the ride\, please visit https://meetup.com/handybikes or htt\r\n ps://handybikesdc.com/for/rides  age. \r\nURL:https://www.handybikesdc.com/articles/rides-classes-events-pg225.htm\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024\r\nLOCATION:3950 Wheeler Avenue\r\nGEO:38.807998;-77.101501\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3950 Wheeler Avenue;X-APPLE\r\n -RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Port City Brewing Company:geo:38.807998,-77.101501\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Port City Brewing Company;DIR=https://www.handybikesdc.com/art\r\n icles/rides-classes-events-pg225.htm:mailto:ryan@portcitybrewing.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 6/01/PedalsAndPints-02_52971CB7-8DB9-41C0-9CE1FC731665E08C_events-150x150.\r\n png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:1b64c782b8d4ccd46078a1cebc54473b\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104600Z\r\nSUMMARY:Joggers & Lagers\r\nDESCRIPTION:Start your week off with a Monday evening run from Port City Br\r\n ewing Company.\nThe run meets at the brewery tasting room before heading o\r\n ut for a 1\, 3 or 5 mile run (it's an out and back route so really it's as\r\n  long as you care to make it). It's a pleasant route through a park and th\r\n en picking up a paved path along Holmes Run.\nExpect a fun crowd\, support\r\n  from Pacers Running staff\, and occasionally vendors will be there with s\r\n hoes to try out on the run.\r\nURL:https://www.portcitybrewing.com/\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026\r\nLOCATION:3950 Wheeler Avenue\r\nGEO:38.807998;-77.101501\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3950 Wheeler Avenue;X-APPLE\r\n -RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Port City Brewing Company:geo:38.807998,-77.101501\r\nORGANIZER;CN=Port City Brewing Company;DIR=https://www.portcitybrewing.com/\r\n :mailto:ryan@portcitybrewing.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 26/01/joggers-lagers-01_1E4B44EB-2D86-4F02-BA1D439CE019D935_events-150x150\r\n .jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:935609efc0c9685cfef4f70684ed00d3\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104558Z\r\nSUMMARY:Union Navy Exhibition Opens at Fort Ward Museum\r\nDESCRIPTION:A new exhibition\, &#x93\;Aboard Ship with the Jack-Tars of the\r\n  Union Navy\,&#x94\; opens October 2 at the City of Alexandria's Fort Ward\r\n  Museum.  The theme focuses on the U.S. Navy during the Civil War\, and i\r\n s being held in recognition of the 250th anniversary of the founding of th\r\n e U.S. Navy on October 13\, 1775.  The exhibition will continue through 2\r\n 026.\nThe Federal Navy\, which began as a small and unprepared force at th\r\n e outbreak of the Civil War\, quickly expanded to succeed in blockading ov\r\n er 3\,500 miles of Confederate coastline\, securing the South's major wate\r\n rways\, and engaging in a number of significant combat operations.  By th\r\n e end of the war in 1865\, the U.S. Navy was the world's largest naval for\r\n ce and a key factor in the North's eventual victory.\nThe strength of the \r\n U.S. Navy would not have been possible without the service of the thousand\r\n s of sailors\, or &#x93\;jack-tars\,&#x94\; who manned the ships.  A typi\r\n cal ship's crew included men and boys of various ages and ethnic backgroun\r\n ds\, including a significant number of Black seamen who served on integrat\r\n ed crews.  The exhibition features examples of the tools\, equipment\, cl\r\n othing articles\, weapons and personal items used by Union sailors from Fo\r\n rt Ward Museum's Civil War collection.  Major themes focus on naval dress\r\n \, which identified men by various ranks and roles\, communications aboard\r\n  ship\, navigation\, and weaponry used in combat.  The exhibition include\r\n s a special profile on Commander James Harmon Ward\, Fort Ward's namesake\\r\n , who was the first Union Navy officer to die in the Civil War.\nFort Ward\r\n  is the best preserved of the extensive system of Union forts that compris\r\n ed the Civil War Defenses of Washington.  Fort Ward Museum and Historic S\r\n ite is located at 4301 West Braddock Road in the City of Alexandria.  For\r\n  more information\, please call 703.746.4848 or visit alexandriava.gov/For\r\n tWard.  \n \n \n \n \r\nURL:https://www.alexandriava.gov/FortWard\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026\r\nLOCATION:4301 W. Braddock Road\r\nGEO:38.830775;-77.101771\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=4301 W. Braddock Road;X-APP\r\n LE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Fort Ward Museum & Historic Site:geo:38.830775,-77.10\r\n 1771\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 5/10/navy-c2l-official_AE8071F7-C645-4290-A4D59B47FC321419_events-150x150.\r\n png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:9aed12fb67950d38e2231f49be3905fe\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104558Z\r\nSUMMARY:Union Navy Exhibition Opens at Fort Ward Museum\r\nDESCRIPTION:A new exhibition\, &#x93\;Aboard Ship with the Jack-Tars of the\r\n  Union Navy\,&#x94\; opens October 2 at the City of Alexandria's Fort Ward\r\n  Museum.  The theme focuses on the U.S. Navy during the Civil War\, and i\r\n s being held in recognition of the 250th anniversary of the founding of th\r\n e U.S. Navy on October 13\, 1775.  The exhibition will continue through 2\r\n 026.\nThe Federal Navy\, which began as a small and unprepared force at th\r\n e outbreak of the Civil War\, quickly expanded to succeed in blockading ov\r\n er 3\,500 miles of Confederate coastline\, securing the South's major wate\r\n rways\, and engaging in a number of significant combat operations.  By th\r\n e end of the war in 1865\, the U.S. Navy was the world's largest naval for\r\n ce and a key factor in the North's eventual victory.\nThe strength of the \r\n U.S. Navy would not have been possible without the service of the thousand\r\n s of sailors\, or &#x93\;jack-tars\,&#x94\; who manned the ships.  A typi\r\n cal ship's crew included men and boys of various ages and ethnic backgroun\r\n ds\, including a significant number of Black seamen who served on integrat\r\n ed crews.  The exhibition features examples of the tools\, equipment\, cl\r\n othing articles\, weapons and personal items used by Union sailors from Fo\r\n rt Ward Museum's Civil War collection.  Major themes focus on naval dress\r\n \, which identified men by various ranks and roles\, communications aboard\r\n  ship\, navigation\, and weaponry used in combat.  The exhibition include\r\n s a special profile on Commander James Harmon Ward\, Fort Ward's namesake\\r\n , who was the first Union Navy officer to die in the Civil War.\nFort Ward\r\n  is the best preserved of the extensive system of Union forts that compris\r\n ed the Civil War Defenses of Washington.  Fort Ward Museum and Historic S\r\n ite is located at 4301 West Braddock Road in the City of Alexandria.  For\r\n  more information\, please call 703.746.4848 or visit alexandriava.gov/For\r\n tWard.  \n \n \n \n \r\nURL:https://www.alexandriava.gov/FortWard\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027\r\nLOCATION:4301 W. Braddock Road\r\nGEO:38.830775;-77.101771\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=4301 W. Braddock Road;X-APP\r\n LE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Fort Ward Museum & Historic Site:geo:38.830775,-77.10\r\n 1771\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 5/10/navy-c2l-official_AE8071F7-C645-4290-A4D59B47FC321419_events-150x150.\r\n png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:f3d2a8a4798c2ed06e1a4db5c091557c\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104558Z\r\nSUMMARY:Union Navy Exhibition Opens at Fort Ward Museum\r\nDESCRIPTION:A new exhibition\, &#x93\;Aboard Ship with the Jack-Tars of the\r\n  Union Navy\,&#x94\; opens October 2 at the City of Alexandria's Fort Ward\r\n  Museum.  The theme focuses on the U.S. Navy during the Civil War\, and i\r\n s being held in recognition of the 250th anniversary of the founding of th\r\n e U.S. Navy on October 13\, 1775.  The exhibition will continue through 2\r\n 026.\nThe Federal Navy\, which began as a small and unprepared force at th\r\n e outbreak of the Civil War\, quickly expanded to succeed in blockading ov\r\n er 3\,500 miles of Confederate coastline\, securing the South's major wate\r\n rways\, and engaging in a number of significant combat operations.  By th\r\n e end of the war in 1865\, the U.S. Navy was the world's largest naval for\r\n ce and a key factor in the North's eventual victory.\nThe strength of the \r\n U.S. Navy would not have been possible without the service of the thousand\r\n s of sailors\, or &#x93\;jack-tars\,&#x94\; who manned the ships.  A typi\r\n cal ship's crew included men and boys of various ages and ethnic backgroun\r\n ds\, including a significant number of Black seamen who served on integrat\r\n ed crews.  The exhibition features examples of the tools\, equipment\, cl\r\n othing articles\, weapons and personal items used by Union sailors from Fo\r\n rt Ward Museum's Civil War collection.  Major themes focus on naval dress\r\n \, which identified men by various ranks and roles\, communications aboard\r\n  ship\, navigation\, and weaponry used in combat.  The exhibition include\r\n s a special profile on Commander James Harmon Ward\, Fort Ward's namesake\\r\n , who was the first Union Navy officer to die in the Civil War.\nFort Ward\r\n  is the best preserved of the extensive system of Union forts that compris\r\n ed the Civil War Defenses of Washington.  Fort Ward Museum and Historic S\r\n ite is located at 4301 West Braddock Road in the City of Alexandria.  For\r\n  more information\, please call 703.746.4848 or visit alexandriava.gov/For\r\n tWard.  \n \n \n \n \r\nURL:https://www.alexandriava.gov/FortWard\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028\r\nLOCATION:4301 W. Braddock Road\r\nGEO:38.830775;-77.101771\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=4301 W. Braddock Road;X-APP\r\n LE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Fort Ward Museum & Historic Site:geo:38.830775,-77.10\r\n 1771\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 5/10/navy-c2l-official_AE8071F7-C645-4290-A4D59B47FC321419_events-150x150.\r\n png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:a0dc079f25483f95b4aae81acc447e4c\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104558Z\r\nSUMMARY:Union Navy Exhibition Opens at Fort Ward Museum\r\nDESCRIPTION:A new exhibition\, &#x93\;Aboard Ship with the Jack-Tars of the\r\n  Union Navy\,&#x94\; opens October 2 at the City of Alexandria's Fort Ward\r\n  Museum.  The theme focuses on the U.S. Navy during the Civil War\, and i\r\n s being held in recognition of the 250th anniversary of the founding of th\r\n e U.S. Navy on October 13\, 1775.  The exhibition will continue through 2\r\n 026.\nThe Federal Navy\, which began as a small and unprepared force at th\r\n e outbreak of the Civil War\, quickly expanded to succeed in blockading ov\r\n er 3\,500 miles of Confederate coastline\, securing the South's major wate\r\n rways\, and engaging in a number of significant combat operations.  By th\r\n e end of the war in 1865\, the U.S. Navy was the world's largest naval for\r\n ce and a key factor in the North's eventual victory.\nThe strength of the \r\n U.S. Navy would not have been possible without the service of the thousand\r\n s of sailors\, or &#x93\;jack-tars\,&#x94\; who manned the ships.  A typi\r\n cal ship's crew included men and boys of various ages and ethnic backgroun\r\n ds\, including a significant number of Black seamen who served on integrat\r\n ed crews.  The exhibition features examples of the tools\, equipment\, cl\r\n othing articles\, weapons and personal items used by Union sailors from Fo\r\n rt Ward Museum's Civil War collection.  Major themes focus on naval dress\r\n \, which identified men by various ranks and roles\, communications aboard\r\n  ship\, navigation\, and weaponry used in combat.  The exhibition include\r\n s a special profile on Commander James Harmon Ward\, Fort Ward's namesake\\r\n , who was the first Union Navy officer to die in the Civil War.\nFort Ward\r\n  is the best preserved of the extensive system of Union forts that compris\r\n ed the Civil War Defenses of Washington.  Fort Ward Museum and Historic S\r\n ite is located at 4301 West Braddock Road in the City of Alexandria.  For\r\n  more information\, please call 703.746.4848 or visit alexandriava.gov/For\r\n tWard.  \n \n \n \n \r\nURL:https://www.alexandriava.gov/FortWard\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261029\r\nLOCATION:4301 W. Braddock Road\r\nGEO:38.830775;-77.101771\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=4301 W. Braddock Road;X-APP\r\n LE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Fort Ward Museum & Historic Site:geo:38.830775,-77.10\r\n 1771\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 5/10/navy-c2l-official_AE8071F7-C645-4290-A4D59B47FC321419_events-150x150.\r\n png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:a11bb640a63041793376142d9842e646\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104558Z\r\nSUMMARY:Union Navy Exhibition Opens at Fort Ward Museum\r\nDESCRIPTION:A new exhibition\, &#x93\;Aboard Ship with the Jack-Tars of the\r\n  Union Navy\,&#x94\; opens October 2 at the City of Alexandria's Fort Ward\r\n  Museum.  The theme focuses on the U.S. Navy during the Civil War\, and i\r\n s being held in recognition of the 250th anniversary of the founding of th\r\n e U.S. Navy on October 13\, 1775.  The exhibition will continue through 2\r\n 026.\nThe Federal Navy\, which began as a small and unprepared force at th\r\n e outbreak of the Civil War\, quickly expanded to succeed in blockading ov\r\n er 3\,500 miles of Confederate coastline\, securing the South's major wate\r\n rways\, and engaging in a number of significant combat operations.  By th\r\n e end of the war in 1865\, the U.S. Navy was the world's largest naval for\r\n ce and a key factor in the North's eventual victory.\nThe strength of the \r\n U.S. Navy would not have been possible without the service of the thousand\r\n s of sailors\, or &#x93\;jack-tars\,&#x94\; who manned the ships.  A typi\r\n cal ship's crew included men and boys of various ages and ethnic backgroun\r\n ds\, including a significant number of Black seamen who served on integrat\r\n ed crews.  The exhibition features examples of the tools\, equipment\, cl\r\n othing articles\, weapons and personal items used by Union sailors from Fo\r\n rt Ward Museum's Civil War collection.  Major themes focus on naval dress\r\n \, which identified men by various ranks and roles\, communications aboard\r\n  ship\, navigation\, and weaponry used in combat.  The exhibition include\r\n s a special profile on Commander James Harmon Ward\, Fort Ward's namesake\\r\n , who was the first Union Navy officer to die in the Civil War.\nFort Ward\r\n  is the best preserved of the extensive system of Union forts that compris\r\n ed the Civil War Defenses of Washington.  Fort Ward Museum and Historic S\r\n ite is located at 4301 West Braddock Road in the City of Alexandria.  For\r\n  more information\, please call 703.746.4848 or visit alexandriava.gov/For\r\n tWard.  \n \n \n \n \r\nURL:https://www.alexandriava.gov/FortWard\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030\r\nLOCATION:4301 W. Braddock Road\r\nGEO:38.830775;-77.101771\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=4301 W. Braddock Road;X-APP\r\n LE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Fort Ward Museum & Historic Site:geo:38.830775,-77.10\r\n 1771\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/202\r\n 5/10/navy-c2l-official_AE8071F7-C645-4290-A4D59B47FC321419_events-150x150.\r\n png\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:e54b686bd7d98449515a7264c6da7008\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104641Z\r\nSUMMARY:AR Workshop Alexandria: 2 HOUR EXPERIENCE - CANDLE POURING + SCENT \r\n MIXOLOGY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Join us for this scent-sational DIY workshop!\nCreate one-of-a-\r\n kind candle scents for your home or as the perfect hand-crafted gift. Enjo\r\n y our classic candle style as well as options to upgrade and add-on during\r\n  your visit. [The more you pour\, the more you save!]\nVisit our homepage \r\n to register. Times Vary by date. \n \n \r\nURL:https://www.arworkshop.com/alexandria/#schedule\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024\r\nLOCATION:1212 King Street\r\nGEO:38.805696;-77.053203\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=1212 King Street;X-APPLE-RA\r\n DIUS=49;X-TITLE=AR Workshop Alexandria:geo:38.805696,-77.053203\r\nORGANIZER;CN=AR Workshop Alexandria;DIR=https://www.arworkshop.com/alexandr\r\n ia/#schedule:mailto:alexandria@arworkshop.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 25/07/Candle-Pouring-Scent-Mixology-Cafeteria-Setup-15_C646A87D-2868-4DF9-\r\n A7A0FE7415027A5A_events-150x150.jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nBEGIN:VEVENT\r\nUID:c202184bcd0bedf60c2e5914930e5418\r\nDTSTAMP:20261024T224355Z\r\nLAST-MODIFIED:20261022T104633Z\r\nSUMMARY:AR Workshop Alexandria: SIGNATURE Wood\, Canvas + Textured Art Work\r\n shop\r\nDESCRIPTION:Join us for this fun-filled DIY workshop!\nCreate a unique home\r\n  decor item utilizing a variety of tools and techniques and our in-house\r\n  collection of paints and non-toxic stains while guided by our crafty in\r\n structors.\nThis is our most popular workshop featuring our Signature Wood\r\n \, Canvas\, and Textured Art projects\, to include plank and framed signs\\r\n , rounds\, trays\, boxes and canvas pillows. This is a 2.5 to 3 hour DIY e\r\n xperience.\nMultiple classes per week. See our full calendar and register \r\n here: https://www.arworkshop.com/alexandria/#schedule\r\nURL:https://www.arworkshop.com/alexandria/#schedule\r\nDTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261029\r\nLOCATION:1212 King Street\r\nGEO:38.805735;-77.053200\r\nX-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=1212 King Street;X-APPLE-RA\r\n DIUS=49;X-TITLE=AR Workshop Alexandria:geo:38.805735,-77.053200\r\nORGANIZER;CN=AR Workshop Alexandria;DIR=https://www.arworkshop.com/alexandr\r\n ia/#schedule:mailto:alexandria@arworkshop.com\r\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\r\nATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitalexandria.com/wp-content/uploads/20\r\n 25/07/arwCharlotte-1170_0FA3DEDD-57B8-44CE-97A979096EDCDD56_events-150x150\r\n .jpg\r\nBEGIN:VALARM\r\nACTION:DISPLAY\r\nDESCRIPTION:Reminder: the event starts in an hour!\r\nTRIGGER;RELATED=END:-PT1H\r\nEND:VALARM\r\nEND:VEVENT\r\nEND:VCALENDAR